It is a fork of Omarchy's built-in `omarchy.agents` bar widget, so that
Claude Code session status can share one bar button with the usage panel
instead of adding a second icon.

From Omarchy, unmodified:

    Agent.qml
    assets/

From Omarchy, with additions marked `[claude-status]`:

    Panel.qml    four additions: the status component, the bar button
                 bindings, the sessions list, and plain-text rendering
                 for the synced model name
    Main.qml     bounds on the synced-snapshot path — allowed sync
                 directories, file and byte caps on the scan, and caps
                 and sanitising on everything parsed out of it

Original to this plugin:

    ClaudeStatus.qml
    ClaudeSessions.qml
    bin/omarchy-claude-status
    setup
    resync
    manifest.identity.json

`resync` re-derives the Omarchy-derived files from the copy of Omarchy
installed on the machine and re-applies those additions, so the fork can be
brought back in line after an `omarchy update`.
